    "body": "Fix status (no PR yet).\n\n- Branch: `qsmits:issue/4085-dinsio-manual-change`\n- Head: `1d70083456fdee7d07d06df619f376ce9eb07f92`\n\n**Sequence that the DIN/ISO post writes.** The machine must state `tooling.tool_change = \"manual-retract-top\"` (the Fehlmann Picomax 55). At each tool change after the first tool, the post writes these blocks:\n\n```\nN210 M5*                     (end of the previous section, as before)\nN230 G00 G90 Z+0 M92*        (retract, under the OLD tool call)\nN240 ; CHECK DRIVES OFF BEFORE TOUCHING TOOL*\nN250 ; CHECK QUILL AT PHYSICAL CHANGE POSITION*\nN260 ; ABORT IF EITHER CHECK FAILS*\nN270 ; THEN INSTALL TOOL 3 FLAT-6*\nN280 M6*                     (the stop: MP 7440 bit 0 = 0)\nN300 T3 G17 S3500*           (the new tool length starts here)\n```\n\n- At the first tool, the post writes the checks and `M6` only, with no move.\n- A repeated tool number writes no stop.\n- The T block comes after the stop. Thus the retract uses the length of the tool that is in the spindle. The M92 target is a machine position, so the move goes only up.\n\n**Engine law.** On a machine with `tooling.tool_change` = `manual` or `manual-retract-top`, a post must list that mode in its manifest (`manualToolChange = [\"manual-retract-top\"]`). If it does not, the engine refuses the post by name, with the post and the machine, before any hook runs.\n\n- `heidenhain.cps` and `heidenhain-klartext.cps` declare `manual-retract-top`.\n- The 24 other shipped posts are refused on the Picomax.\n- Plain `manual` refuses the DIN/ISO post too, because that mode states no change position.\n- Machines without a manual change do not change: all goldens are byte-identical, and there is one new golden (`picomax_two_tools.nc`).\n\n**Gate on head `1d7008345`** (log first line `1d70083456fdee7d07d06df619f376ce9eb07f92`):\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 310 steps, 0 failed. This includes `example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive` and `example_catalog_edge_work`.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: 6 steps, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Targeted heavy step `cargo xtask gate heavy --base origin/main --only \"app heavy: example_catalog\"`: ok, 4 passed.\n\nPinning tests are in `crates/post/tests/script_heidenhain.rs`, module `picomax`. The decision is in `docs/decisions/4085-heidenhain-din-manual-change.md`.\n\nNo run on the real control was done.\n\nPR to be opened in the morning.\n",
